@page "/"

<PageTitle>Phophi's Azure App</PageTitle>

<div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
        <span class="badge">Cloud Development A • First Azure Deployment</span>
        <h1>Hi, I’m Phophi 👋🏾</h1>
        <p class="intro">
            Welcome to my first .NET web application deployed to Microsoft Azure App Service.
            This project marks the beginning of my cloud development journey, where I am learning
            how to build, deploy, and manage applications in the cloud.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-buttons">
            <a class="primary-btn" href="https://coco-cloud-dev.azurewebsites.net" target="_blank">Live App</a>
            <a class="secondary-btn" href="https://github.com/PDzivhani/cloud-dev-a-azure-app" target="_blank">GitHub Repo</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="features">
    <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>☁️ Azure App Service</h3>
        <p>
            I used Azure App Service to host and deploy this application in the cloud.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>💻 .NET 8 + Blazor</h3>
        <p>
            This app was built using .NET and Blazor, giving me practical experience with modern web development.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>🚀 First Deployment</h3>
        <p>
            This was my first successful deployment from my local machine to a live Azure environment.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="journey-section">
    <h2>Why this project matters</h2>
    <p>
        This is more than a tutorial app. It represents my first hands-on step into Azure cloud development
        and my commitment to growing as a developer who can build real-world cloud-based applications.
    </p>
</section>